{"id":"54dcb8a12b227069244ca219","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/fred-nile-former-nsw-politician-and-figurehead-of-the-rightwing-christian-democratic-party-dies-aged-92","published_at":"2026-11-22T00:26:35Z","collected_at":"2026-11-22T01:43:25.678155Z","title":"Fred Nile, former NSW politician and figurehead of the rightwing Christian Democratic party, dies aged 92","text":"Fred Nile retired from politics after unsuccessfully contesting the 2023 election. Photograph: Dan Himbrechts/AAP View image in fullscreen Fred Nile retired from politics after unsuccessfully contesting the 2023 election. Photograph: Dan Himbrechts/AAP New South Wales politics Fred Nile, former NSW politician and figurehead of the rightwing Christian Democratic party, dies aged 92 Controversial figure frequently took positions against drug use, abortion and homosexuality, but in later years supported legislation expunging homosexual convictions Get our daily political email , free app or daily news podcast Ben Smee Sat 21 Nov 2026 19.26 EST Last modified on Sat 21 Nov 2026 19.51 EST Share Prefer the Guardian on Google The former New South Wales MP and longstanding figurehead of the rightwing Christian Democratic party, the Rev Fred Nile, has died aged 92. Nile was a member of the NSW legislative council for more than 40 years. He first entered the state’s upper house in 1981 and retired after unsuccessfully contesting the 2023 election. Nile was a controversial figure; a standard-bearer for Christian and social conservative politics since long before the formation of the Australian","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/4d437bc81d1032afb812de5027b40b3c646fa358/288_0_3708_2967/master/3708.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/10b4e02333ee97ecf51d5e814fd324a88832fb17/1177_0_2998_3000/2998.jpg?width=100&dpr=2&s=none&crop=1%3A1"],"author":"Ben Smee","l